Title: Baker's Dozen

INT. DINER – DAY

Christmas season. A worn vinyl booth. Police officers sit across the aisle. Low diner chatter, cutlery clinks, faint Christmas music.

JOHN, blond and muscular, sits opposite STEVE, scrawny and impatient. Both wear tan work shirts. Two strips of bacon on John's plate. Coffee in Steve's hand.

Steve sips his coffee and sets it down hard.

STEVE
(fast, irritated)
Best fucking burger joint in Shat City, and you order eggs with bacon.

Steve jabs a finger at the plate.

STEVE
Then you leave it sitting there like a fucking Christmas ornament.

JOHN
(calm)
I like the smell.

STEVE
What?

JOHN
(completely sincere)
Eggs don't smell good alone. Bacon evens it out.

Steve stares, speechless.

Steve sighs, exhausted.

STEVE
How many takes is this?

John slowly turns and looks directly into the camera.

JOHN
(completely sincere)
As many as you want. It's Script F-X.

Steve stares at John, confused. Hold. Neither smiles.
